<!--
    Test dataset for VisitSummaryPdfExportControllerTest.

    Drives the whole visit-summary pipeline end to end: REST controller -> report ->
    dataset evaluator -> section SPI -> XML renderer -> XSL-FO -> PDF bytes. Every
    section that ships with the module contributes data for visit 9001, so the
    generated PDF can be text-extracted and asserted against.

    IDs are deliberately high (90001+/91001+) so nothing collides with
    standardTestDataset (max concept_id 5497) or with the api-module section datasets.

    Concept classes come from standardTestDataset:
      1 = Test (lab), 3 = Drug, 4 = Diagnosis, 5 = Finding (vitals), 11 = Misc,
      19 = Frequency
    Concept datatypes: 1 = Numeric, 3 = Text, 4 = N/A.

    Patient 90001 "Mercy Aine Nakato" — the fully-populated patient:
      Visit 9001 at "Kayunga Health Centre III", one encounter, and
        vitals      : systolic 128 / diastolic 84 (combined), heart rate 76 bpm
        labResults  : Glucose 9.5 mmol/L, interpretation HIGH, normals 4-7
        visitNotes  : one note obs attributed to a Clinician-role provider
        diagnoses   : Malaria, CONFIRMED, rank 1
        conditions  : Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, ACTIVE, onset 2023-02-01
        allergies   : Penicillin, Severe, reaction Rash
        medications : active drug order for Lisinopril 5 mg Oral Twice daily, 10 days

    Patient 90002 "Silent Empty Kirya" — the empty-visit edge case:
      Visit 9002 has no location, no encounters, and the patient has no allergies,
      conditions or drug orders, so every data section must fall through to its
      "None recorded" empty state and the PDF must still render.

    The role/privilege rows below give the stock (non-superuser) "butch" user the
    "Get Visits" privilege but NOT "App: Can generate a Visit Summary", so the
    privilege-denied path can be exercised with a real user rather than a mock.
-->
